  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}$ are vectors such that $\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}+\\vec{c}=0$ and $|\\vec{a}|=7,|\\vec{b}|=5,|\\vec{c}|=3$ then angle between vector $\\vec{b}$ and $\\vec{c}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$60^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$30^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$45^{\\circ}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$90^{\\circ}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}+\\vec{c}=0 \\Rightarrow \\vec{b}+\\vec{c}=-\\vec{a} \\Rightarrow(\\vec{b}+\\vec{c})^2=(\\vec{a})^2=5^2+3^2+2 \\vec{b} \\vec{c}=7^2$\n$\\Rightarrow 2|\\vec{b}||\\vec{c}| \\cos \\theta=49-34=15 \\Rightarrow 2 \\times 5 \\times 3 \\cos \\theta=15 \\Rightarrow \\cos \\theta=1 / 2 \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{3}=60^{\\circ}$"
  }
}